<title>USA: U.S. CHAIN STORE SALES OFF 0.5 PCT - BTM/SCHRODERS.</title>
<headline>U.S. CHAIN STORE SALES OFF 0.5 PCT - BTM/SCHRODERS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. chain store sales slipped 0.5 percent in the week ended August 9 from the prior week, according to the seasonally adjusted BTM/Schroders weekly chain store sales index.</p>
<p>Sales for the week were down 2.8 percent on a year-over-year basis, while the month-to-date index dropped 0.2 percent from the prior month.</p>
<p>&quot;August chain store sales are expected to post a 5.5 percent year-over-year gain,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
